# Architecture Rules

- Use only `Backend/src/` — never legacy backend folders outside `src`
- Respect layered architecture: Domain → Application → Infrastructure → API
- Controllers must stay thin; business logic belongs in Application services
- State changes must use `OrderStatusStateMachine` / `OrderStatusTransitionHelper`
- All DTOs must enforce role masking; never expose client/designer sensitive data
- Backend authorization is mandatory (`[Authorize]`, roles, `[RequirePermission]`, service-level access checks)
- Use async everywhere for I/O
- Validate all uploads (`UploadSecurityHelper`, revision/file rules)
- Never trust frontend permissions — re-validate on API
- Use structured logging (Serilog)
- Avoid large components/services; prefer reusable abstractions (helpers, shared access rules)
